# UI translations (da + en)

User-facing text belongs in the UI layer only. Keep Danish and English in sync.

## Where strings live

- Messages: `client/src/i18n/messages/da.ts` and `client/src/i18n/messages/en.ts`
- Components use `useLocale()` → `t('key.path')` (and interpolation like `{{version}}` when needed)
- Do not hardcode Danish or English UI copy in JSX/TSX
- Do not put locale strings in the server API, models, or AI service layer for product UI

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
<Button>Gem</Button>

// ✅ GOOD
const { t } = useLocale();
<Button>{t('common.save')}</Button>
```

## When adding UI text

1. Add the same key to both `da.ts` and `en.ts`
2. Use the key via `t(...)` in the component
3. Prefer nested keys that match the feature (`nav.*`, `settings.*`, etc.)

Server may return stable machine values (status codes, enum keys). The client maps those to translated labels.
